SRC/sifi -- sifi, as built for OS-9/68000=========================================sifi writes the plot of a science fiction film: who attacks the Earthor is discovered, what they want, and how it ends.  `sifi -3' writesthree and ends with `The End.'; `sifi' alone writes one.  Written byKevin D. Quitt, posted to alt.sources on 30 July 1990, and de-ansifiedby chad@anasaz.UUCP.  The author notes that the flowchart it follows wasnot his, and believes it was Gahan Wilson's, published in OMNI around1981.  From the `silly' collection posted to alt.sources in December1992.ORIG holds sifi.c as posted, and sifi.sp, a rules file for `spew' madefrom the same plots by wiml@milton.u.washington.edu in 1990.sifi.c is unchanged and builds as posted, taking its K&R declarations;rand() is linked from /dd/LIB/rand.r.sifi.sp is not usable with this disk's spew.  It was written for amodified spew that was not posted with it: it names a class `SIFI!',which spew rejects with `Bad class header: %SIFI!', and it uses a\PRUNE pseudo-class that spew does not have.